{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"obj1","type":"objection","text":"The account mistakes strategic ambiguity for accidental ambiguity.","target":"rec1","bearing":"If the ambiguity is intentional, a written system (rec4) only changes the medium of the dispute rather than resolving the motive."},{"id":"obj2","type":"objection","text":"The account assumes the avoiding party's motive is overwhelm or lack of safety.","target":"rec3","bearing":"If the motive is resentment or strategic avoidance, reframing as a system problem (rec5) bypasses the necessary emotional resolution."},{"id":"prob1","type":"problem","text":"How to distinguish between a coordination failure (systemic) and a cooperation failure (interpersonal) before selecting a remedy?"}],"uptake":[]}